summary:
  A settle round that runs out of reads without a verdict just stops.

history:
  The round after a rebuild has five reads to make a verdict of three.
  Ten refusals at the gate end it with a line, and so does a probe that
  refuses every retry. Reads spent on answers that could not be read, or
  were skipped, or never came, ended it with nothing. On 2026-11-11 the
  five probes after a restart all came back unsteady between 18:20 and
  18:28; the round was over, the room was 50 ms out and stayed there
  until 21:50, and the journal read as if the round were still going.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
          if (_settleReadsLeft <= 0) { console.log(SyncJournal.settleOver(_settleEarsRuns.length)); return; }

replace:
          if (_settleReadsLeft <= 0) return;

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_sync_journal.py::test_a_settle_round_whose_probes_all_came_back_unreadable_says_it_is_over.
  Line-neutral.
